description:
Objective:
Replace the cli placeholder with a thin entry that consumes core (`buildBanner`,
`main` printing version + resolved config). Proves epic acceptance #1: CLI consumes
core, and core builds with zero cli dependency.

Files:
- Modify: `packages/cli/src/index.ts`
- Test:   `packages/cli/test/cli.test.ts`

Steps:

1. Write the failing test `packages/cli/test/cli.test.ts`:
```ts
import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';
import { buildBanner } from '../src/index.js';

describe('cli', () => {
  it('builds a banner that includes the core version', () => {
    expect(buildBanner('1.2.3')).toBe('Loreweaver — core v1.2.3');
  });
});
```

2. Run it to verify FAIL.
   Command: `npx vitest run packages/cli/test/cli.test.ts`
   Expected: FAIL — `buildBanner` is not exported (current export is `placeholder`).

3. Replace `packages/cli/src/index.ts` entirely with:
```ts
import { CORE_VERSION, ConfigError, loadConfig } from '@loreweaver/core';

export function buildBanner(version: string): string {
  return `Loreweaver — core v${version}`;
}

export function main(): void {
  console.log(buildBanner(CORE_VERSION));
  try {
    const cfg = loadConfig();
    console.log(`db=${cfg.campaignDbPath} model=${cfg.model}`);
  } catch (err) {
    if (err instanceof ConfigError) {
      console.error(`config error: ${err.message}`);
      process.exitCode = 1;
      return;
    }
    throw err;
  }
}

if (import.meta.url === `file://${process.argv[1]}`) {
  main();
}
```

4. Run the test to verify PASS.
   Command: `npx vitest run packages/cli/test/cli.test.ts`
   Expected: 1 passed.

5. Build everything, then prove core has zero cli dependency: build ONLY core
   from a clean state.
   Command: `npm run build && rm -rf packages/core/dist packages/cli/dist && npm run build --workspace @loreweaver/core`
   Expected: exit 0; `packages/core/dist/index.js` exists and core build never
   references `@loreweaver/cli` (core has no such import/dependency).

6. Run the full test suite.
   Command: `npm test`
   Expected: all tests pass; the model integration test is skipped (no API key).

7. Commit.
   Command: `git add -A && git commit -m "feat(e0): thin CLI consuming core (boundary proven)"`
